Steps for running simulations
-----------------------------

Ensure that the following variables are set as per the user's
local environment settings.

eg : setenv GLOBAL /h/arm/global

eg : setenv DIRS_VERILOG /AVANT/1999.1/cb25/v2.1/verilog/cb25os163/zero

eg : setenv FILES_VERILOG /AVANT/1999.1/cb25/v2.1/verilog/cb25os163/zero/mtb_verilog.v

eg : setenv LIB_SYNOP /AVANT/1999.1/cb25/v2.1/synopsys/cb25os163/1997.01/models

Please note that the above paths are EXAMPLE paths.

setenv PERIPH Smc

Additionally, set the following environment variables to control
simulations using a modelsim simulator.

RTL Simulations
---------------
setenv SIMULATOR modelsim
setenv HDL_SOURCE verilog

NETLIST Simulations
-------------------
setenv SIMULATOR modelsim
setenv TEST_METH noscan
setenv HDL_SOURCE vhdl
setenv HDL_NETL verilog

Set the following environment variables to control simulations using a
LDV simulator.

setenv SIMULATOR LDV
setenv TEST_METH scanready
setenv HDL_SOURCE verilog
setenv HDL_NETL verilog

1. VERILOG RTL simulations (For both modelsim and LDV simulators)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
   - In the integration/bustest directory 'make <testname>'
     where <testname> refers to the specific test vector set
     that needs to be used for simulations.

     [Please refer to integration/bustest/makefile for the
      complete list of <testname>s.]

     This will create integration/bustest/invec/tif.sim

   - In the integration/verilog directory
     'make rtl'

2. VERILOG NON-SCAN NETLIST simulations (For modelsim simulator)
----------------------------------------------------------------
   - In the integration/bustest directory 'make <testname>'
     where <testname> refers to the specific test vector set
     that needs to be used for simulations.

     [Please refer to integration/bustest/makefile for the
      complete list of <testname>s.]

     This will create integration/bustest/invec/tif.sim

   - In the integration/verilog directory
     'make net_min'

     This will perform a MINIMUM timing annotated simulation
     on the VERILOG netlist generated from VHDL RTL.

3. VERILOG SCANREADY NETLIST simulations (For LDV simulator)
------------------------------------------------------------
   - In the integration/bustest directory 'make <testname>'
     where <testname> refers to the specific test vector set
     that needs to be used for simulations.

     [Please refer to integration/bustest/makefile for the
      complete list of <testname>s.]

     This will create integration/bustest/invec/tif.sim

   - In the integration/verilog directory
     'make net_typ'

     This will perform a TYPICAL timing annotated simulation
     on the scanready VERILOG netlist generated from VERILOG
     RTL.

